	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12829"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=946" title="View the profile of Leayrn">Leayrn</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 8<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/dancegiri.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								VIVA LA BARDY~<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=946"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1201.msg12829#msg12829"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1201.msg12829#msg12829">Re: Christmas Contest</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #2 on:</b> November 25, 2004, 06:39:18 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Hello, my name is Leayrn and I&#039;m an al....CRAP wrong opening! <br />Everquestaholic would be more like it, although I havn&#039;t played for a month or so due to monetary issues :/ I&#039;m here to represent the guild Outcast Adventurers, which for some odd reason I&#039;ve been a member of for over a year and a half now. <br />Anyways <br />should this entry win, I would like to defer choice of the mob taken down to my guild leader Cudget. Honestly, when it comes to progression, I don&#039;t know much except for the basics. Besides, he knows a lot better what we need to to take down than I do...I&#039;m just here for the entertainment. All I know is that pizza is good...mmmmyes, you know what I&#039;m talking about, when you wake up and you have that half eaten pizza in the fridge from the raid the night before? Oh yeah... <br /><br /><i>  Leayrn leaned against the bar at the tavern that she and her guild had taken residence in after their latest planar venture.  They had just taken out Sol Ro himself, and they deserved a bit of enjoyment after that trial.  She had come so far since she had joined these companions...it was almost unbelievable</i><br /><br />A little bit about myself before I go on. My name is Leayrn, the artist formerly known as Danny, singer of songs, weaver of tales, and drinker of waaaaaaaaay too much ale *burp* I started out in this grand adventure called Everquest about 2 and a half years ago, learning about the orcs and the bees around the n00b lift in Gfay. Gettin cozy with the guards, ya know? Still swear to this day that he has a thing for me, he helped me out so many times...Anyways. Ya know, back then, I really didn&#039;t expect to become a slavering game junkie....*shrug* In the end, i guess, it&#039;s not the game, but my guild that makes me renew my subscription...no, really *points to the gun that Rony is holding to his head* About 2 weeks and 7 levels into my gaming, I ran across a guy that was doing open recruiting for &quot;Rodcet&#039;s Fury&quot;, a lowbie guild at the time. I accepted, because having a guild name was UBER. I stayed in that guild for about 2-3 months I think, making friends and becoming more and more addicted to this game. Eventually though, that guild broke down, and I had to move on. <br />Then I met the guild that made me want to play EQ more...Knights of the Sacred Grove. Some of the friendliest people I&#039;ve ever met are still currently in this guild, and it was such a blast being in that guild. I knew everyone, and they all knew &quot;The Black Bard!&quot; because back then, I kept all my armor dyed black. Even that had to end eventually though...I outgrew KSG, and had to move on from there, so I could start seeing more of the game. My friend Sansegrall recommended that I app to his guild. That was a year and a half ago, and I&#039;m still proudly in that guild...Outcast Adventurers. <br /><i>When she had joined this guild, she was so inexperienced in the ways of the world of Norrath.  These people had showed her so much, and she owed each and every one of them not only her life, but her friendship as well.  She took one last sip of her ale, and waded out into the dancing crowd, reveling in the feeling.</i><br /><br />Joining the new guild wasn&#039;t as much of a change as I thought it would be. KSG was really really family oriented, but they didn&#039;t raid...at all. I think, every great now and then, we&#039;d go pwn crushbone, but that was it. <br />Although it was cool paying that bastige Dvinn back for all those times he....errr where was I? <br />Oh yeah. OA has that social sense as well, but..we raid too. And that first night, raiding is something I&#039;d never done except for that little 3 month period doing OWD raids (yeah, I&#039;m sure over half the server remembers those, with scrotaur cursing week after week because he&#039;d constantly lose on the cloak of flames....ahh memories) So here I am, with a group of OA sitting in the Umbral Plains, a level 55 bard wearing a full suit of Lambent armor. I felt soooo embarassed because everything they were letting rot was a BIG upgrade for me, but I was still having fun...and then I got to see the dreaded &quot;rogue pull&quot;. I was sitting there, and I saw in the raid channel &quot;Umm...zone.&quot; I looked out, and I saw cudget run by with like, half the zone on him? I about crapped myself! <br /><br />I remember that...and then I think of how we are now...Elemental flagged...and it just completely blows my mind that I can remember getting our butt kicked my Rumblecrush or Doomshade, and now we could walk in there, fart, and they&#039;d die..we do have our off days on raids still though. We have days where just, everyone seems to be out of it, not wanting to follow orders or anything. But then again, we can turn around, and on our next attempt kill something flawlessly...that&#039;s just the way OA is. If we fail at first, give us another try, because every time we fail it just makes our resolve harder to win, and generally, the second or third time (if it&#039;s a brand new raid mob) we take it down. That&#039;s honestly one of the best memories I have, is the night when we took down Terris Thule. We killed her on our second try, and everyone was sooo happy because we had finally taken the first real step to planar progression...I felt like I had accomplished something. <br /><br />All in all, the people who are in the guild, not the events that occured, provide the fondest memories in my EQ life. Hell, some of them didn&#039;t even occur in the game! It&#039;s just from talking and hanging out with people that I&#039;ve gotten to know on a day to day basis. Sure, there have been bad times, or people that have made my own personal blacklist, but those are by far the minority.  I can tell that it all works for me...why?  Because after 2 years, almost 300 dollars or so, I&#039;m *still* here.  And my guild is a very big part of it.  Through all the crap, all my issues in my personal life, my friends have always been there.  And whenever times are tough, we always live by one phrase.<br /><br />Blame the rogue!!!<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
