						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg12883"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=330" title="View the profile of Faelin">Faelin</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Leader<br />
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 9<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=330"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.brewmasters.org" title="Brew Masters" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1201.msg12883#msg12883"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1201.msg12883#msg12883">Re: Christmas Contest</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #3 on:</b> November 30, 2004, 01:06:36 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							It&#039;s the last day to submit for this and we drunkards at the Brew Master Guild hall were lazy and waited till the last minute. This fun little poem was written by Grohmk the Ogre Warrior, long time Brew and all around fun guy. We call him &quot;Heavy Grohmk&quot; at his request - drunk Ogres generally get what they want.<br /><br />You might notice that it&#039;s written to the meter and spirit of &quot;A Night Before Christmas&quot; (that being anapestic tetrameter). Grohmk is a great poet but if he deviates that meter, forgive us we&#039;ll ration his Brew.<br /><br /><hr /><br />Twas the night before patch day, and all through the guild,<br />excitement aflutter, our hearts it did fill;<br />While Averse and Faelin did plan out the raids,<br />Rhus snooped through folks’ pockets, just trying to get paid.<br /><br />Many of the guildies, complained about classes:<br />“Sony sucks at balancing!  They sit on their asses!”<br />But still others insisted upon questing and grinding,<br />or just staring at wood elves, with rear-ends so blinding.<br /><br />Lumnos and Mooni, power couple extraordinaire,<br />sat sighing over Mayn, as she complained about her hair.<br />“I’M NOT QUITE COMFORTABLE WITH THIS!,” Mayn did exclaim,<br />as Maxo made jokes that were increasingly lame.<br /><br />And Blackrose’s corpses did clog every zone<br />to the point where Sony added “/hidecorpse all” to try and atone.<br />He’s not a bad pally, his skills are quite uber <br />(though you might not expect it from such a kind-hearted goober).<br /><br />Old Gravelox sat snickering atop his horse, Binky,<br />at Trashcan the ogre’s emissions so stinky.<br />And Abrahms, the Barb with his obsession for sheep,<br />put warm water on Mamsong’s hand as he was trying to sleep.<br /><br />While easy to guess the result of Abe’s prank, <br />we’d only be rewarding him if we gave him a spank.<br />So the guild house was filled with that litterbox smell,<br />despite Bieroth’s repeatedly praying to Brell.<br /><br />But one thing in common, with all of the Brews,<br />was booze-laden bellies, and partying too.<br />Regardless however, those Brews sure can raid!<br />(We need something to do if we’re not getting laid;-))<br /><br />The next morning, “Listen up!,” the raid leaders said,<br />but half of the Brews were hung-over in bed.<br />Thus is the life of the truest of Brews, <br />to drink and to drink til you fall from your shoes.<br />Nevertheless, the leaders kept on,<br />until most of the raid targets were already gone.<br /><br />They talked and they talked, and then talked a bit more, <br />til most of the Brews passed out on the floor.<br />But finally, “We have a target!” they exclaimed,<br />“We need to kill Rallos for fortune and fame!”<br /><br />So Azlani the monk, with man-boobs a-flying<br />began to bring pulls to the raid who was trying<br />to fight through the headaches and nausea from booze, <br />and all of the whining, complaints and boo-hoos.<br /><br />“Now Tallon!” the raid leaders finally said, <br />“Then Vallon as soon as this bastard is dead!”<br />So we dodged giant arrows, and multiple swords<br />and made our way forward to the big wooden door<br />where the mighty Rallos Zek, in his huge dining hall<br />was ready to kick BM square in the….teeth.<br />And finally, when that first Rallos Zek fell dead,<br />The second Rallos’ zonewide shout filled us with dread.<br /><br />So Sibaelius and Samaara and the rest of the nukers<br />MGB teleported all those snoozers and pukers.<br />We rushed right back into that so-deadly pit<br />where Rallos Zek the Warlord would soon pop us like a zit.<br /><br />We tried our damndest to handle those adds<br />but the evil hangovers were just way too bad.<br />So rezzing began in the Tactics graveyard,<br />and the guild exclaimed, “Man, that sucker was hard!”<br /><br />But never discouraged, Brew will try again<br />and without any doubt, we know we will win.<br />The elemental planes will never be the same<br />when BM comes crashing, to slaughter and maim.<br /><br />So look out, Sol Ro, cause we’ll come for you too!<br />We’ll smack you with swords, spells, and even kung-fu!<br />Cause nothing can stop Brew from winning the day<br />Not even Frig’s cyb0ring will get in our way!<br /><br />So to put an end to this epic story,<br />we WILL earn our way to power and glory,<br />and we would be honored, if those that once were Brews<br />but moved to DA and EiE too,<br />would help us along in our time of need-<br />Matil and Korosha will you lend us your speed?<br />Vendy and Lexr, we could use your help too!<br />Robb, Benlie, and Nialid, is there something you’ll do?<br /><br />But these friendships reaffirmed would be the greatest reward;<br />greater than spells, armor, jewelry ,or swords.<br />For why do we remain in the world of Norrath,<br />if loot is the object at the end of our path?<br />The relationships that we form in the time that we spend,<br />the laughter, the tears, and the lifelong friends,<br />the memories that will last until Norrath’s no more,<br />these are the reasons deep down at the core.<br />We continue to play, day in and day out,<br />because friendship is what EQ is really about. <br /><br />- Heavy Gromhk RoninHeart, Overlord of Brew Masters.<br /><hr /><br /><br />This is the official submission of the Brew Masters Guild, right here on Rodcet Nife.<br />&nbsp;<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cool.gif" alt="Cool" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
